  "name": "fun-with-threads",
  "description": "A comparative performance study of multi-threaded synchronization primitives implemented in C and Rust. It benchmarks various strategies for protecting shared state—including mutexes, spinlocks, and atomic operations—against baseline race conditions. The project utilizes flamegraphs to visualize and analyze the performance overhead and contention characteristics of each concurrency model.",
